{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120005","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120005/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120005/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120005/events","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/120005","id":4585000271,"node_id":"I_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABEUmNTw","number":120005,"title":"Flickering light on mesh in Compatibility when two lights (one frustrum culled) shine on the same MultiMeshInstance","user":{"login":"tldmbruno","id":118130235,"node_id":"U_kgDOBwqGOw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/118130235?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno","html_url":"https://github.com/tldmbruno","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tldmbruno/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","color":"ff6055","default":true,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708289,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:3d","name":"topic:3d","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2026-06-04T01:33:14Z","updated_at":"2026-06-22T09:32:09Z","closed_at":"2026-06-22T09:32:03Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in 4.6.3.stable in Compatibility rendering mode.\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.3.stable - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce GT 710 (NVIDIA; 30.0.14.7514) - Intel(R) Xeon(R) CPU E5-2640 v3 @ 2.60GHz (16 threads) - 15.84 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nLights from 3D positional lights (such as OmniLight3D or SpotLight3D) will flicker if one of them is frustum culled while the other is not, while both of them shine upon a MultiInstanceMesh. What I think it happens is the mesh appears to suffer some kind of \"light_energy-fighting\" (like a Z-fighting but with light) while trying to render the bright side of the mesh with both the occluded and non-occluded light, during Compatibility mode.\n\nThis problem has nothing to do with any of the OpenGL light count limits, nor shadow casting (since it doesn't include shadows).\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Switch to Compatibility mode\n2. Place 2 Omnilight3D in a scene, far apart, both shining upon a big MultiMesh\n3. Place the camera between both lights, far enough so the camera cannot see any of the light coming from behind\n4. The received light from the non-occluded light will flicker upon the MultiMesh\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120005/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":2},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120005/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"not_planned","pinned_comment":null}